Throw std::bad_alloc directly instead of calling the libstdc++ internal

std::__throw_bad_alloc() is a libstdc++ implementation detail that GCC 16,
which freedesktop-sdk 26.08 ships, no longer declares in <bits/functexcept.h>,
so jemalloc_cpp.cpp stops compiling. Upstream made the same change; drop this
patch once a release carries it.

diff --git a/src/jemalloc_cpp.cpp b/src/jemalloc_cpp.cpp
--- a/src/jemalloc_cpp.cpp
+++ b/src/jemalloc_cpp.cpp
@@ -100,7 +100,7 @@ handleOOM(std::size_t size, bool nothrow) {
 	}
 
 	if (ptr == nullptr && !nothrow)
-		std::__throw_bad_alloc();
+		throw std::bad_alloc();
 	return ptr;
 }
 
